  "slug": "detection-cytometry-f0fb",
  "summary": "Immune scATAC mapping of about 280,000 cells shows caQTLs explain roughly 50% more GWAS loci than eQTLs, motivating regulatory-level analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is statistical and computational machinery for high-dimensional epigenomic and molecular data, in which the analysis must respect the structure of the measurement. MELODY extends logistic-regression mediation analysis to high-dimensional omics mediators with a binary outcome and introduces an R2-like total mediation measure. SACOMA applies an unsupervised, data-adaptive, spatially constrained hierarchical clustering framework to identify co-methylated regions in DNA methylation array data, so spatial organization shapes the grouping. The published study is a different kind of contribution: a unified scATAC map of roughly 280,000 immune cells from 48 individuals, including 20 with COVID-19, identifies 37,390 caQTLs that explain about 50% more GWAS loci than eQTLs. The dominant thread is methodological, and only the two preprints share it directly. Together, the items connect explicit modeling of dependence and spatial structure with regulatory variation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-15"
}
